cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PeerReviewAgents"
abstract: >-
  PeerReviewAgents is a multi-agent framework for structured manuscript review
  with large language models. A default run converts a PDF locally, applies an
  optional desk screen, and sends the manuscript to eight specialist reviewers
  covering methodology, data analysis, novelty, clarity, literature, rigor,
  reproducibility, and ethics. Two parallel auditors check methods completeness
  and citation support. An advocate and skeptic debate the reviews before an
  area chair prepares a synthesis, a simulated author responds, and an editor
  issues an accept, minor revision, major revision, or reject recommendation.
  A journal scout can then suggest publication venues. Agents return typed
  Pydantic outputs, and each run writes the individual reports, synthesis,
  decision letter, usage records, and configuration needed to inspect the
  process. The framework supports OpenRouter, Anthropic, and OpenAI providers,
  along with a terminal interface, headless command-line execution, and a web
  interface. Optional research tools query scholarly literature sources, while
  target-journal settings and revision rounds support venue-specific and
  follow-up review. The system is research software for review assistance and
  evaluation, not a substitute for accountable editorial judgment.
type: software
